---
// The meta row of the deep-dive archetype: a wrapping mono line of small
// facts under a heading or above the way out. Two devices render it — the
// article meta line (date, update date, tags) and the destination links of a
// case study — and they must go on rendering the same one, which is why the
// declarations sit here once rather than twice.
//
// `gap: 8px 16px` is row then column, so it is `gap-y-2 gap-x-4`: the wider
// gap separates items on a line, the narrower one separates wrapped rows.
// Reading those two the wrong way round is a change nobody would call a bug
// and nobody would call intended either.
//
// A `<p>` and not a `<ul>`, deliberately: a `<ul>` start tag closes an open
// `<p>`, and the chips this line carries are a list nested inside it. Anything
// a caller puts here must be phrasing content for the same reason.
---

<p
  class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mbs-6 font-mono text-size-eyebrow text-muted"
><slot /></p>
